WEBVTT

00:44.336 --> 00:45.421
Eui-ju!

00:45.504 --> 00:46.839
CHAPTER 26:
YOU'RE AN OUTLIER

00:54.638 --> 00:55.931
Are you in pain, miss?

00:56.766 --> 00:58.267
Are you Ms. Yeo's guardian?

00:58.350 --> 00:59.185
Yes.

00:59.268 --> 01:01.520
How long has she been sweating like this?

01:01.604 --> 01:04.190
-About 30 minutes.
-Does she often suffer abdominal pain?

01:04.273 --> 01:06.984
-I'm not sure.
-Okay.

01:07.067 --> 01:09.278
Will you please wait in the waiting room?

01:09.361 --> 01:10.196
Is it serious?

01:10.279 --> 01:11.572
-Just wait for now.
-All right.

01:11.655 --> 01:12.990
Doctor, it's an emergency.

01:13.073 --> 01:14.158
Let me check you over.

01:14.241 --> 01:15.117
It hurts.

01:15.201 --> 01:16.410
-It hurts here?
-Yes.

01:16.494 --> 01:18.162
What about here? Does it hurt a lot?

01:18.245 --> 01:19.997
Let's take her
to the emergency treatment room.

01:20.080 --> 01:21.457
Let's go.

01:21.540 --> 01:23.000
EMERGENCY ROOM
ENTRY RESTRICTIONS

01:43.145 --> 01:46.398
Anyone going in there
falls under one of just two categories.

01:47.274 --> 01:48.400
It must be serious.

01:48.984 --> 01:50.110
The poor thing.

01:51.612 --> 01:52.446
"Serious"?

01:53.072 --> 01:55.032
HANA UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

02:24.562 --> 02:26.313
Is Yeo Eui-ju's guardian here?

02:27.314 --> 02:28.607
Yes, that's me.

02:40.494 --> 02:41.495
Mr. Ga.

02:42.663 --> 02:44.665
What am I going to do now, Mr. Ga?

02:45.541 --> 02:46.375
I should've known.

02:46.458 --> 02:48.377
I did wonder about

02:48.460 --> 02:50.963
why I've lost my appetite
and been suffering from indigestion.

02:52.047 --> 02:53.549
I saw a case like mine on TV.

02:53.632 --> 02:55.593
Acute leukemia.

02:56.552 --> 02:59.221
Even people who appear healthy
get struck down like this.

02:59.847 --> 03:03.183
But if you collapse suddenly like this,
it means you don't have long to live.

03:04.059 --> 03:05.477
I'm…

03:05.561 --> 03:08.397
I'm only 18 years old.

03:09.106 --> 03:10.482
When I became an adult,

03:10.566 --> 03:13.360
I wanted to buy an R-rated novel
in my own name

03:14.153 --> 03:17.448
and load my account up with 100,000 won
at a time and read whatever I wanted.

03:18.741 --> 03:19.992
Mr. Ga.

03:21.619 --> 03:22.578
I…

03:25.039 --> 03:26.874
I have a bad feeling about this.

03:27.499 --> 03:28.876
I really think…

03:28.959 --> 03:30.961
Are you feeling better?

03:33.255 --> 03:34.340
What's wrong with her?

03:34.423 --> 03:35.466
Here you are, doctor.

03:35.549 --> 03:36.425
Oh, dear.

03:36.508 --> 03:39.219
All right. Let's take a look
at your X-ray together.

03:39.845 --> 03:43.849
You can see here.
It's been building up for quite a while.

03:43.933 --> 03:46.560
Not good at all.

03:46.644 --> 03:48.812
Why didn't you come in sooner?

03:49.772 --> 03:52.566
Mr. Ga, what am I going to do?

03:52.650 --> 03:53.692
Oh, my.

03:53.776 --> 03:55.235
It's okay. It won't be that serious.

03:55.319 --> 03:58.364
Mr. Ga, I don't want to die.

03:58.447 --> 03:59.490
Don't worry. Hush now.

03:59.573 --> 04:00.950
-What do I do?
-They can treat you.

04:01.033 --> 04:02.284
Please call my mom.

04:02.368 --> 04:04.411
They can treat you. You will be fine!

04:06.246 --> 04:08.832
Please call my mom.

04:10.250 --> 04:11.251
Is it a serious illness?

04:11.752 --> 04:13.337
She had constipation.

04:18.759 --> 04:19.593
Sorry?

04:22.096 --> 04:23.263
But…

04:24.348 --> 04:27.434
Can constipation cause you to pass out?

04:27.518 --> 04:28.936
Shouldn't you run more tests?

04:29.019 --> 04:30.312
She was full to bursting.

04:30.396 --> 04:33.899
All the white you see here is stool.

04:36.360 --> 04:38.362
We gave her an enema.

04:38.445 --> 04:41.115
And this is how you look now.

04:41.198 --> 04:43.701
Isn't that nice and clean?

04:45.703 --> 04:48.038
When you get home,

04:48.122 --> 04:49.665
why don't you try weighing yourself?

04:51.208 --> 04:53.085
You're free to leave.

05:07.808 --> 05:09.601
Please just leave, Mr. Ga.

05:10.310 --> 05:12.980
I'll make my own way home.

05:13.063 --> 05:14.732
Please just leave without another word.

05:14.815 --> 05:15.649
Please.

05:17.985 --> 05:19.987
Why aren't you going?

05:20.070 --> 05:22.406
Please just leave.

05:22.489 --> 05:23.699
Right now.

05:24.867 --> 05:25.993
I will never get…

05:27.870 --> 05:28.954
how you…

05:30.164 --> 05:31.081
always manage…

05:33.876 --> 05:36.170
to prove yourself to be an outlier.

05:43.427 --> 05:44.386
I'm off.

05:59.068 --> 06:00.527
Shall I just transfer?

06:02.905 --> 06:03.739
Oh, my.

06:03.822 --> 06:05.157
Eui-ju!

06:05.783 --> 06:07.451
-Where is she?
-Eui-ju!

06:07.534 --> 06:09.578
-Eui-ju!
-Eui-ju!

06:09.661 --> 06:10.829
-Eui-ju!
-I'm fine.

06:10.913 --> 06:12.748
-Eui-ju!
-Does it hurt a lot?

06:12.831 --> 06:14.416
Mom, I want to transfer.

06:14.500 --> 06:15.334
Transfer?

06:18.087 --> 06:20.506
EPISODE 8

06:23.050 --> 06:26.095
Why do you think
Woo-su changed his mind about filming?

06:27.012 --> 06:28.639
He must have been blackmailed.

06:28.722 --> 06:31.600
Do you know how scary the principal is?

06:31.683 --> 06:33.268
Her expression can change in an instant.

06:33.352 --> 06:35.270
He's not the type to give in to blackmail.

06:35.854 --> 06:36.897
-Right.
-Sure.

06:36.980 --> 06:38.273
-Yeah.
-You got that right.

06:38.899 --> 06:41.068
What has she got on him?

06:42.111 --> 06:44.029
He's home.
You'd better apologize properly.

06:44.113 --> 06:45.989
Okay already.

06:49.284 --> 06:50.953
You're late. You haven't had dinner yet?

06:53.455 --> 06:55.749
I'll go get some rice.
You can get the soup.

07:02.297 --> 07:03.173
Great work today.

07:05.050 --> 07:06.510
Is that it?

07:06.593 --> 07:08.470
Didn't you have something to say to him?

07:12.349 --> 07:14.017
I'm sorry about earlier.

07:14.768 --> 07:15.644
About what, exactly?

07:16.854 --> 07:18.522
Dude, can't you just accept my apology?

07:23.235 --> 07:24.236
Well.

07:28.115 --> 07:28.991
You know.

07:30.576 --> 07:31.952
I'm sorry that I went behind your back

07:32.828 --> 07:34.955
to have you filmed
when I knew you hated it

07:37.124 --> 07:39.376
and brushed off your past trauma
like it was nothing.

07:43.964 --> 07:45.174
At least you know.

07:45.257 --> 07:46.466
What about cutlery?

07:46.550 --> 07:48.677
Right. I'll get it.

07:50.512 --> 07:51.388
You're so cool.

07:55.684 --> 07:57.144
Don't you have anything to say to me?

07:59.146 --> 08:01.148
I won't call you fruit bat
for the next month.

08:01.231 --> 08:02.900
Can you just not call me that at all?

08:02.983 --> 08:04.860
-What do you think?
-You totally can, glasses monkey!

08:04.943 --> 08:06.153
-Jeez, you fruit bat.
-Hey!

08:06.236 --> 08:08.739
Did you hear that? He just did it!

08:09.823 --> 08:10.824
He said he wouldn't!

08:10.908 --> 08:12.201
I never pinky-promised.

08:14.578 --> 08:15.537
I'm not eating anymore.

08:16.496 --> 08:18.207
-Why the heck am I a fruit bat?
-Suit yourself.

08:22.336 --> 08:25.547
I thought I was done
with embarrassing myself.

08:38.477 --> 08:40.270
Eui-ju!

08:40.354 --> 08:41.730
So broad,

08:42.773 --> 08:44.024
so warm…

08:45.567 --> 08:46.944
and so cozy.

09:28.902 --> 09:30.487
According to a study
on constipation in teens

09:32.030 --> 09:34.533
and related factors,

09:35.117 --> 09:38.078
the top three causes of constipation are

09:38.161 --> 09:42.124
low levels of physical activity at 43%,
excessive instant food intake at 24.6%,

09:42.207 --> 09:43.834
and irregular sleep patterns at 16%.

09:43.917 --> 09:47.462
I assume these contributed
to the unfortunate incident yesterday.

09:48.171 --> 09:49.840
I'll keep that in mind.

09:49.923 --> 09:51.425
Thank you for yesterday.

09:51.508 --> 09:53.593
I'm not religious,
but it was a weird feeling.

09:54.261 --> 09:57.306
I bestowed grace upon the student
who betrayed me.

10:05.897 --> 10:08.191
How backed up were you
that you had to go to the ER?

10:08.942 --> 10:10.736
It's because you don't drink enough water.

10:10.819 --> 10:13.071
Your poop gets hard like stones
and won't come out.

10:13.155 --> 10:14.573
What? Wait, no.

10:14.656 --> 10:15.866
Are you okay, Eui-ju?

10:15.949 --> 10:17.200
I hear you went to the ER.

10:19.578 --> 10:22.539
How could you hold it in
until it got that bad?

10:23.290 --> 10:25.042
You're definitely a bit slow.

10:25.667 --> 10:27.419
Oh, and thanks for yesterday.

10:27.502 --> 10:28.378
Mr. Noh.

10:30.047 --> 10:32.841
What was that about yesterday?
You said you knew something.

10:34.384 --> 10:35.218
What?

10:36.636 --> 10:38.847
You said you knew my secret.

10:39.681 --> 10:40.724
What would I know?

10:46.688 --> 10:47.856
I can totally see the change.

10:47.939 --> 10:49.483
You're looking a lot better today.

10:56.615 --> 10:57.449
What the heck?

10:58.784 --> 11:00.077
Did he trick me?

11:01.787 --> 11:04.623
So the math teacher
hasn't spilled the beans about my novel?

11:08.210 --> 11:11.129
Hey, Eui-ju!
Going to the ER with constipation?

11:11.213 --> 11:12.214
That's no big deal!

11:12.297 --> 11:13.840
There's no need to feel embarrassed!

11:13.924 --> 11:15.550
Just make sure you poop properly!

11:15.634 --> 11:16.593
You got this, Eui-ju!

11:17.177 --> 11:18.553
Constipation is no joke!

11:18.637 --> 11:20.263
All right, fine. See you!

11:29.606 --> 11:30.732
-Oh A-rin.
-Here.

11:30.816 --> 11:32.192
CHAPTER 27:
LIKE A CAT, LITTLE BY LITTLE

11:32.275 --> 11:34.027
-Choi Yu-mi.
-Here.

11:34.111 --> 11:35.487
-Yeo Eui-ju.
-Here.

11:36.571 --> 11:37.989
-Choi Go-ya.
-Here.

11:38.073 --> 11:39.074
Choi Ji-a.

11:50.293 --> 11:51.503
-Hong Su-min.
-Here.

11:52.129 --> 11:53.213
-Jeon Chae-won.
-Here.

11:53.296 --> 11:54.714
-Im Su-yeon.
-Here.

11:55.799 --> 11:57.092
-Jenny.
-Here.

11:58.844 --> 12:01.304
Give it your all in class today.
Have a good one.

12:01.388 --> 12:03.140
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

12:03.223 --> 12:04.307
Eui-ju, come with me.

12:15.444 --> 12:16.528
Why isn't Ji-a here?

12:17.446 --> 12:19.114
I don't know.

12:20.240 --> 12:23.535
When I asked about Ji-a on day one,
you were the only one who answered.

12:23.618 --> 12:24.995
Want to guess how I interpreted it?

12:26.663 --> 12:31.960
I thought that with your help,
she might feel more positive about school.

12:32.544 --> 12:35.338
She might even change.
That made me trust you.

12:38.967 --> 12:41.303
I want you to step up your game
and try to help her.

12:41.386 --> 12:43.638
Let's say you know
someone is waiting for you at school.

12:43.722 --> 12:45.015
Even if you hated it,

12:45.098 --> 12:46.766
you'd still drag yourself here,
wouldn't you?

12:48.518 --> 12:51.480
The thing is, the way I see it,

12:51.563 --> 12:54.691
Ji-a is not the kind of girl
you can just go up to.

12:54.774 --> 12:57.611
What I mean is, she's just like a cat.

12:58.278 --> 13:02.699
You have to creep up to her cautiously,
little by little.

13:05.660 --> 13:06.661
Try that, then.

13:09.331 --> 13:10.874
But you're getting four demerits today.

13:11.791 --> 13:13.835
Are you going to betray my trust?

13:13.919 --> 13:15.003
No, sir.

13:23.386 --> 13:25.639
What on earth…

13:28.558 --> 13:30.644
Damn you, Ji-a.

13:32.145 --> 13:33.813
Ji-a's absent again.

13:33.897 --> 13:34.940
Tell me about it.

13:36.066 --> 13:39.152
By the way, why is she always by herself?

13:40.320 --> 13:41.488
I'm not sure.

13:41.571 --> 13:44.616
Some people just prefer
keeping themselves to themselves.

13:44.699 --> 13:45.534
Maybe she's one.

13:46.993 --> 13:50.956
To be honest, I find her a bit scary.

13:51.039 --> 13:53.750
Feels like things will kick off
if I rub her the wrong way.

13:55.252 --> 13:58.505
Come on, she's not much of a talker,
but she's not like that.

13:58.588 --> 14:00.507
She was in my class in tenth grade.

14:00.590 --> 14:03.969
I remember she always picked up
a chalk that fell on the floor.

14:04.052 --> 14:07.013
Oh, and whereas other kids
found it a pain to do the recycling,

14:07.097 --> 14:09.891
she would stay behind alone
to take care of it.

14:10.809 --> 14:11.810
So…

14:12.602 --> 14:15.272
There are people
who favor actions rather than words.

14:15.355 --> 14:16.856
I think that's her style.

14:18.149 --> 14:19.150
Here she is now.

14:22.654 --> 14:23.488
There you are.

14:24.656 --> 14:25.699
You could've come earlier.

14:27.242 --> 14:29.160
Why were you late today?

14:47.721 --> 14:51.099
MURIM GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL

14:52.225 --> 14:54.603
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

14:58.607 --> 15:01.026
Let's turn to page 280.

15:01.109 --> 15:02.152
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir.

15:07.240 --> 15:11.411
We're celebrating the literature month
with a poetry and art exhibition.

15:12.287 --> 15:14.205
Each class has to select a representative.

15:14.289 --> 15:16.374
Does anyone want to try writing a poem?

15:20.670 --> 15:22.380
Sir, Eui-ju's your girl.

15:22.464 --> 15:23.798
She's an amazing writer.

15:24.382 --> 15:25.967
Yeah, she's always
working on some project.

15:26.051 --> 15:28.011
She even won
a creative writing prize last year.

15:31.306 --> 15:34.851
Really? Then she can be
your class representative.

15:35.435 --> 15:36.853
Is that okay, Eui-ju?

15:37.479 --> 15:39.356
Okay, I'll do it.

15:39.981 --> 15:41.858
Sir, can Go-ya help out by drawing?

15:41.941 --> 15:43.151
Sounds great.

15:43.234 --> 15:45.403
Is that okay, Go-ya?

15:46.946 --> 15:49.532
Sure, anything I can do to help.

15:50.116 --> 15:53.119
Then class two will be represented by
Yeo Eui-ju and Choi Go-ya.

15:55.538 --> 15:56.665
Looking forward to it.

15:56.748 --> 15:58.792
-Yes, sir.
-Yes, sir. We'll do our best.

16:12.681 --> 16:13.973
Are you in detention for demerits?

16:15.517 --> 16:16.643
Yes, sir.

16:16.726 --> 16:18.895
I never know when I might get more.

16:18.978 --> 16:20.271
So I have to work them off.

16:21.773 --> 16:22.899
Did you have lunch?

16:23.566 --> 16:24.567
Yes. How about you, sir?

16:24.651 --> 16:25.652
I did too.

16:27.946 --> 16:29.072
Eui-ju.

16:29.155 --> 16:30.073
Yes?

16:35.954 --> 16:40.417
Mr. Ga knows
you weren't filming him the other day.

16:41.584 --> 16:42.419
Really?

16:43.837 --> 16:46.339
Then why is he being so hard on me?

16:50.385 --> 16:51.678
It must be because of his glasses.

16:52.721 --> 16:53.596
His glasses?

16:54.848 --> 16:55.807
Yes.

16:55.890 --> 16:58.309
I had his glasses

16:58.393 --> 16:59.728
back when he lost them.

17:00.311 --> 17:01.896
You had them?

17:03.773 --> 17:04.607
Yes.

17:05.942 --> 17:07.235
Didn't he tell you?

17:07.819 --> 17:09.028
He never said anything.

17:09.904 --> 17:10.739
What the heck?

17:11.364 --> 17:15.076
I thought he would've trashed me
to his friends for throwing them out.

17:15.160 --> 17:19.038
Anyhow, I don't think
he's holding a grudge against you.

17:19.122 --> 17:20.248
So don't get too upset.

17:20.331 --> 17:23.126
Okay. Thanks for looking out for me.

17:23.793 --> 17:27.714
I think it's so cool
you're a published writer.

17:27.797 --> 17:29.758
It's nothing.

17:29.841 --> 17:31.968
I've just enjoyed writing poetry
since middle school.

17:32.552 --> 17:34.929
I started off casually
like I was writing in a diary,

17:36.014 --> 17:39.350
putting into words the emotions
I couldn't keep bottled up.

17:41.895 --> 17:44.355
I had a fair share of failures
with the Spring Literary Contest

17:45.148 --> 17:47.317
until a literary magazine
luckily picked up my piece.

17:48.526 --> 17:50.695
Of course, I still doubt myself even now,

17:52.113 --> 17:53.823
wondering if my writing is good enough.

17:54.741 --> 17:55.575
Still,

17:56.201 --> 18:00.872
eventually, I realized that writing is
all about putting my heart into it.

18:05.335 --> 18:07.128
To tell the truth,

18:07.796 --> 18:11.174
I've written several novels.

18:11.758 --> 18:12.717
Really?

18:13.718 --> 18:14.761
That's so cool.

18:14.844 --> 18:15.845
Not at all.

18:18.139 --> 18:22.268
Sir, how can I write a really great novel?

18:29.609 --> 18:33.446
Make sure each character
has their own voice.

18:35.406 --> 18:36.699
I think that's important.

18:38.952 --> 18:43.373
Each character
should have their own voice?

18:45.333 --> 18:46.334
Yes.

18:47.210 --> 18:48.586
That's so profound.

18:51.506 --> 18:53.508
Now, I'm really looking forward
to your submission.

18:53.591 --> 18:54.425
Oh, come on.

19:22.328 --> 19:23.538
You went to the snack bar?

19:25.164 --> 19:26.332
Yeah.

19:26.416 --> 19:27.500
I would've gone with you.

19:28.126 --> 19:29.043
Thank you.

19:30.169 --> 19:31.129
Where have you been?

19:31.713 --> 19:34.549
Huh? I had a chat with Mr. Yoon.

19:35.341 --> 19:37.677
Hey, he's so amazing.

19:37.760 --> 19:40.096
He started writing poems in middle school.

19:40.179 --> 19:42.932
He had no luck
with Spring Literary Contests,

19:43.016 --> 19:45.310
but he got his big break
through another channel.

19:46.728 --> 19:49.731
I'll do my best with the piece
for our exhibition.

19:49.814 --> 19:52.609
That way,
your brilliant picture will shine.

19:52.692 --> 19:54.485
We'll show everyone

19:55.528 --> 19:57.113
what an amazing artist you are.

19:57.196 --> 19:58.865
Shoot, I'm so nervous.

20:03.161 --> 20:04.787
Should we work on a title first?

20:04.871 --> 20:05.830
No.

20:06.789 --> 20:10.209
CHAPTER 28: I'M GOING TO TRY
TO UNDERSTAND IRRATIONAL NUMBERS

20:13.004 --> 20:15.214
FILES FOR MR. GA
REAL FILES

20:18.676 --> 20:19.677
Okay.

20:19.761 --> 20:20.720
FILES FOR MR. GA

20:23.598 --> 20:25.934
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

20:41.032 --> 20:41.991
WOO-SUUUUUUUU

20:43.993 --> 20:45.244
This won't do.

20:45.870 --> 20:47.747
I'm skipping this, dang it.

20:48.456 --> 20:49.415
Let's move on for now.

20:51.042 --> 20:52.168
I'm not feeling it.

20:52.251 --> 20:53.419
REAL FILES

20:58.132 --> 20:59.467
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

21:06.432 --> 21:07.976
JUST THEN, SOMEONE GRABBED…

21:11.396 --> 21:14.565
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

21:15.566 --> 21:17.026
Why haven't you come to my place lately?

21:17.694 --> 21:19.195
YOON'S EYES WIDEN IN SURPRISE.
IT'S SI-ON

21:19.946 --> 21:21.072
I can't.

21:21.155 --> 21:23.116
No, I don't want to.

21:23.700 --> 21:25.451
Can you pass discrete math by yourself?

21:25.535 --> 21:27.829
You'll flunk without my help.

21:28.663 --> 21:29.914
I'll figure it out by myself.

21:31.332 --> 21:32.333
I'll pay you.

21:35.211 --> 21:36.170
What?

21:36.254 --> 21:37.547
You need money.

21:38.214 --> 21:39.799
I'll pay you to come to my house.

21:41.050 --> 21:42.593
Isn't that why you go to Tae-ha's?

21:43.469 --> 21:44.554
It's not like that.

21:45.138 --> 21:46.180
Yes, it is.

21:46.264 --> 21:47.974
How is that punk any different from me?

21:48.057 --> 21:49.392
Tae-ha is nothing like you.

21:50.643 --> 21:52.562
And how exactly is he different?

21:53.563 --> 21:56.482
Ultimately, he's also using money
to make you do what he wants.

21:57.650 --> 22:00.570
You're poor, so instead of money, you'll
have to find another way to repay me.

22:01.195 --> 22:02.196
That ten million won.

22:03.281 --> 22:04.741
Pay me back properly.

22:08.786 --> 22:09.829
Fine, take it out on me.

22:10.538 --> 22:11.873
Go ahead, keep your pride.

22:12.415 --> 22:13.708
But in the end, you'll take it.

22:14.584 --> 22:17.003
I'm curious how much your pride is worth.

22:18.671 --> 22:20.214
Why are you going this far?

22:21.090 --> 22:23.009
Do you have to bring me down like this?

22:24.260 --> 22:25.595
Do I seem like a pushover to you?

22:25.678 --> 22:27.889
Don't waste your breath
and come up with a number.

22:29.265 --> 22:31.768
You're going to regret this.

22:32.477 --> 22:34.103
You're really going to regret this.

22:34.604 --> 22:35.605
No.

22:36.272 --> 22:37.648
I'll never regret it.

22:37.732 --> 22:38.941
Not even to my dying day.

22:41.319 --> 22:42.779
END OF EPISODE 5

22:46.783 --> 22:47.909
"Save."

22:53.122 --> 22:53.956
FILES FOR MR. GA

22:59.796 --> 23:00.838
You can do it.

23:01.589 --> 23:02.507
Okay, Eui-ju?

23:03.382 --> 23:04.217
You've got this.

23:05.510 --> 23:06.844
I can't seem to stop yawning.

23:06.928 --> 23:08.387
I need to get home and crash.

23:08.471 --> 23:10.181
You'd need to eat first.

23:10.264 --> 23:11.682
What are we going to eat?

23:11.766 --> 23:13.810
No idea. I'll have to think about it.

23:13.893 --> 23:15.436
Something crispy and warm.

23:15.520 --> 23:18.314
-Jeez, you're so fussy.
-Crispy!

23:18.397 --> 23:19.232
We've got some curry.

23:19.315 --> 23:20.525
-Curry?
-Yeah, from the other day.

23:20.608 --> 23:21.442
You guys go ahead.

23:22.944 --> 23:24.737
-Where are you going?
-Library.

23:25.696 --> 23:26.989
He's always off to the library.

23:27.657 --> 23:29.200
Be home in time for dinner!

23:31.994 --> 23:34.539
Does the school library
have anything at his level?

24:06.654 --> 24:08.197
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 5

24:14.245 --> 24:15.788
From now on,

24:15.872 --> 24:17.748
I'll be your personal bitch.

24:19.292 --> 24:20.334
This isn't like you.

24:20.418 --> 24:21.419
Oh yeah?

24:21.502 --> 24:22.378
EPISODE 5, FOR MR. GA

24:22.461 --> 24:23.296
What am I like, then?

24:23.379 --> 24:25.131
You never cared about me.

24:25.214 --> 24:28.718
You only did a 180
after I became close to Tae-ha.

24:29.302 --> 24:31.304
Are you jealous or something?

24:32.430 --> 24:33.306
Jealous?

24:34.098 --> 24:35.600
Me? Jealous?

24:40.521 --> 24:41.439
Damn right I am!

24:42.315 --> 24:44.108
All that icy treatment was just an act

24:44.192 --> 24:45.526
to hide how I felt about you.

24:46.110 --> 24:48.446
But seeing you with Tae-ha
is driving me crazy.

24:49.822 --> 24:51.199
It's too late.

24:52.200 --> 24:53.492
Get it together, Yoon!

24:54.869 --> 24:57.163
Without me, there's no one left for you.

24:57.830 --> 24:58.998
You have no other choice.

24:59.081 --> 24:59.957
Without me,

25:00.625 --> 25:02.168
you've got nothing!

25:09.217 --> 25:10.843
END OF EPISODE 5

25:21.312 --> 25:22.688
What's the matter, Mr. Ga?

25:23.648 --> 25:25.191
Don't you like it?

25:50.216 --> 25:52.718
I wrote him as an obsessive top.

25:52.802 --> 25:54.303
What doesn't he like about it?

26:10.152 --> 26:12.613
Jeez, he still has his glasses taped up.

26:15.283 --> 26:16.367
What are you staring at?

26:18.244 --> 26:21.414
I was wondering if you'd got new glasses.

26:22.456 --> 26:23.833
My order's not ready yet.

26:25.167 --> 26:26.460
They must be really expensive.

26:27.128 --> 26:29.714
I'm sorry I couldn't buy them for you.

26:30.548 --> 26:31.841
Are you sorry for what happened?

26:32.842 --> 26:33.843
Of course.

26:35.428 --> 26:37.305
What about giving up on math?

26:39.932 --> 26:40.850
That too.

26:49.525 --> 26:50.693
Write how you want to.

26:53.279 --> 26:54.405
Sorry?

26:55.156 --> 26:57.491
Write your own version,
not what I tell you.

26:58.451 --> 26:59.744
Really?

26:59.827 --> 27:00.786
That's amazing.

27:00.870 --> 27:01.871
Is this for real?

27:10.296 --> 27:13.049
To tell the truth, after you caught me,

27:13.132 --> 27:15.468
I thought it was game over.

27:15.551 --> 27:17.386
I figured that was it for me.

27:18.721 --> 27:22.808
Why are you allowing me to write again?

27:33.069 --> 27:36.280
To Pythagoras, the square root of two
was an abnormal number.

27:37.865 --> 27:38.824
Sorry?

27:39.867 --> 27:41.160
What's that got to do with it?

27:41.243 --> 27:44.580
Back then, the only numbers
they could calculate were natural numbers.

27:44.663 --> 27:47.500
Anything that couldn't be expressed
as a fraction was considered irrational.

27:47.583 --> 27:50.669
Such numbers were to be rejected
and not even thought of.

27:52.129 --> 27:54.340
I get why the Pythagoreans were shaken.

27:54.924 --> 27:57.802
Hippasus, who discovered
the square root of two,

27:57.885 --> 27:59.553
died in suspicious circumstances.

28:00.763 --> 28:02.723
They killed him over that?

28:04.892 --> 28:07.436
No one knows who killed him.
It's just a theory.

28:07.520 --> 28:10.564
Wow, Pythagoras was scary.

28:15.611 --> 28:16.946
What do irrational numbers really mean?

28:18.781 --> 28:20.241
It's "irrational" numbers, right?

28:21.075 --> 28:23.536
I believe that things
that appear irrational or illogical

28:23.619 --> 28:25.246
still deserve our time and attention.

28:25.329 --> 28:29.333
I won't repeat Pythagoras's mistake
and dismiss something

28:29.417 --> 28:30.751
just because it seems irrational.

28:33.254 --> 28:35.381
Could you put that in layman's terms?

28:42.513 --> 28:44.557
I'm going to try to understand
irrational numbers.

29:17.756 --> 29:20.509
Fangirling used to be my only joy in life.

29:20.593 --> 29:22.178
-But now…
-Are you okay?

29:22.261 --> 29:24.555
The fact he keeps cropping up in my mind…

29:24.638 --> 29:25.473
It makes me mad.

29:25.556 --> 29:27.433
-I don't want to think about him.
-Let's go.

29:27.516 --> 29:29.602
I shouldn't think about him,

29:29.685 --> 29:31.061
but I can't help myself.

29:31.145 --> 29:33.898
You're into someone,
but you don't want to admit it.

29:33.981 --> 29:35.065
You're in denial.

29:35.149 --> 29:38.194
No matter how much you deny it,
you're already into him.

29:38.277 --> 29:40.571
No. No way.

29:40.654 --> 29:42.114
I shouldn't even like him,

29:42.198 --> 29:43.324
and I just can't.

29:43.908 --> 29:46.577
The guy you like isn't Mr. Jung, is it?

29:47.411 --> 29:49.038
They've gotten really close.

30:47.846 --> 30:49.848
Subtitle: Paul Carver
